// Analyzed file list for opentitan_spi_device_fifo. Paths are relative to the
// PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as cwd
// and `slang` is run from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd. Do not add a trailing `-y`/library directive after the file list --
// an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// ORDER MATTERS for the packages: OpenTitan declares struct types in `_pkg`
// files and uses them in PORT declarations, so a package has to be analyzed
// before the module whose ports it types. The package block below is in
// dependency order and should stay that way.
//
// `ft/opentitan_spi_device_fifo_ft.sv` closes with `default_nettype wire`, so
// an appended worker file is compiled under the default net type and not under
// the `none` that the formal top sets for itself.

// OpenTitan's own configuration switch, and it is LOAD-BEARING. `prim_assert.sv`
// takes the DUMMY macro set under SYNTHESIS, which turns every `ASSERT/`ASSUME
// embedded in the upstream RTL into nothing. Without it spid_upload's three
// `ASSUME`s (CmdFifoNeverFull_M, AddrFifoNeverFull_M, PayloadNeverFull_M) and
// prim_fifo_async_sram_adapter's RSramRvalidOneCycle_M become live constraints
// on the proof, which is a DIFFERENT task from the one this package states --
// two of them assume away exactly the overflow the occupancy targets are about.
+define+SYNTHESIS

// The `include path for prim_assert.sv, prim_assert_dummy_macros.svh,
// prim_assert_sec_cm.svh, prim_flop_macros.sv, prim_macros.svh,
// prim_fifo_assert.svh and prim_util_memload.svh. Those seven are NOT listed
// below: they are macro files reached by `include only, exactly as the upstream
// flow reaches them.
+incdir+rtl

// --- packages, in dependency order, byte-identical upstream OpenTitan --------
rtl/prim_util_pkg.sv
rtl/prim_mubi_pkg.sv
rtl/prim_count_pkg.sv
rtl/prim_ram_2p_pkg.sv
rtl/prim_ram_1r1w_pkg.sv
rtl/spi_device_reg_pkg.sv
rtl/spi_device_pkg.sv

// --- prim cells, byte-identical upstream OpenTitan ---------------------------
// prim_buf / prim_flop / prim_flop_en / prim_flop_2sync / prim_clock_mux2 /
// prim_ram_1r1w / prim_ram_2p are the GENERIC technology variants
// (hw/ip/prim_generic/rtl), which is what the upstream simulation and FPV flows
// pick up. The xilinx and asap7 trees carry same-named modules that instantiate
// vendor cells.
rtl/prim_buf.sv
rtl/prim_flop.sv
rtl/prim_flop_en.sv
rtl/prim_cdc_rand_delay.sv
rtl/prim_flop_2sync.sv
rtl/prim_sec_anchor_buf.sv
rtl/prim_clock_mux2.sv
rtl/prim_count.sv
rtl/prim_pulse_sync.sv
rtl/prim_sync_reqack.sv
rtl/prim_sync_reqack_data.sv
rtl/prim_leading_one_ppc.sv
rtl/prim_arbiter_ppc.sv
rtl/prim_arbiter_tree.sv
rtl/prim_fifo_sync_cnt.sv
rtl/prim_fifo_sync.sv

// The two asynchronous FIFOs. `prim_fifo_async` is the classic gray-pointer
// FIFO with its own storage; `prim_fifo_async_sram_adapter` is the same
// pointer machinery with the storage moved into the dual-port SRAM. Both are
// what this package is about.
rtl/prim_fifo_async.sv
rtl/prim_fifo_async_sram_adapter.sv

rtl/prim_sram_arbiter.sv

// The SECDED encoders/decoders are reached through `prim_ram_*_async_adv`'s
// ECC generate arms. This package runs with EnableECC 0 and EnableParity 1, but
// the other arms still elaborate and have to be on the list.
rtl/prim_secded_inv_39_32_enc.sv
rtl/prim_secded_inv_39_32_dec.sv
rtl/prim_secded_inv_hamming_39_32_enc.sv
rtl/prim_secded_inv_hamming_39_32_dec.sv

rtl/prim_ram_1r1w.sv
rtl/prim_ram_1r1w_async_adv.sv
rtl/prim_ram_2p.sv
rtl/prim_ram_2p_async_adv.sv

// --- spi_device, byte-identical upstream OpenTitan ---------------------------
rtl/spid_csb_sync.sv
rtl/spid_fifo2sram_adapter.sv
rtl/spid_addr_4b.sv
rtl/spi_s2p.sv
rtl/spi_p2s.sv
rtl/spi_cmdparse.sv
rtl/spid_status.sv
rtl/spid_jedec.sv
rtl/spid_upload.sv
rtl/spid_dpram.sv

// --- the oracle and its targets, the covers, and the formal top --------------
sva/targets_opentitan_spi_device_fifo.sv
sva/covers_opentitan_spi_device_fifo.sv
ft/opentitan_spi_device_fifo_ft.sv
